This photo really sums up what the L’horta Downhill Club team is all about—hard work within a united crew where even our beloved KA is part of it and helps make all of this possible. A week later, we’re still exhausted from all the work that went into it. With a core team of just five people (plus collaborators), we managed to organize—and we believe successfully—our third event.
From L’horta, we want to thank all the attendees. We hope the event met your expectations and that you enjoyed it even more than we did. Overall, the vibes were really positive. We’re aware of our shortcomings, but we assure you that we put our heart and soul into making sure everyone enjoys a great weekend of freeride, racing, and of course that slide jam that brings so much spectacle.
We’d like to give some special mentions to all those parts that aren’t always seen but make this possible:
The marshals: A key piece—without you, the runs don’t even start. Thank you!
@cndownhill : A special mention here to @enumbert and @eldar_the_giant dear friends… THANK YOU! The work you do is exceptional. High-quality racing at its best.
@mia_cullera : Thank you for continuing to give us the opportunity year after year and for trusting us.
@natalysanoja : She worked as a marshal (turn 1), helped with setup and teardown, took care of us and kept us fed—you’ve definitely earned a place in heaven. THANK YOU.
@llakatasan : Thank you for all that selfless work—your effort on the poster and those footstops that were such a hit. THANK YOU for all your help.
And to all our sponsors… THANK YOU. Every one of you contributes your grain of sand and helps raise the overall quality of the event.
Not much more to add—the L’horta team, @mdb1422 , @andreu_greses , @ripo_rpg , @xusogr , and @darwinson_magnetic , can only say thank you for everything.
See you next year??

